<title>SOUTH AFRICA: BA cancels more SAfrica flights after strike.</title>
<headline>BA cancels more SAfrica flights after strike.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc said on Tuesday that disrupton caused by last week's 72-hour strike by cabin crew had forced it to cancel further flights to and from South Africa this week.</p>
<p>The cancelled services from London are to Johnnesburg on Wednesday night and to Cape Town on Thursday night. As a result, BA57 from Johannesburg to London on Thursday night and BA58 from Cape Town on Friday night have had to be cancelled.</p>
<p>The company said passengers would be accommodated on other flights.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
